---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import config from "../../site.config";
import { disclaimer } from "@uaeprop/site-kit";
---
<Base title="Terms" description="What Property Desk is, what its numbers are and are not, and the limits of relying on them." path="/terms">
  <div class="col" style="padding-block: var(--space-l) var(--space-xl);">
    <h1>Terms</h1>

    <h2 style="margin-top: var(--space-l);">We are not a broker</h2>
    <p style="margin-top: var(--space-s);">{disclaimer(config.brand)}</p>
    <p>
      Nothing here is an offer to sell property, an invitation to buy one, or an
      advertisement for any specific unit. We hold no Dubai Land Department
      advertising permit because there is nothing here to advertise.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin-top: var(--space-l);">Published data, not advice</h2>
    <p style="margin-top: var(--space-s);">
      This site reports what was registered with the Dubai Land Department and
      published as open data. It is not legal, financial or tax advice, it does
      not know your circumstances, and it cannot see the contract in front of
      you. Before committing, take advice from someone qualified who can.
    </p>
    <p>
      A community median is not a valuation of any property in that community.
      It covers every building, age, floor and finish there at once, and the
      spread within a single community is frequently wider than the gap between
      two of them. Do not read a community figure as a price for a specific
      home.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin-top: var(--space-l);">Figures go out of date</h2>
    <p style="margin-top: var(--space-s);">
      The register is republished continually and this site is rebuilt from it
      periodically, not live. Every figure carries the date of the most recent
      sale behind it. Treat what you see as indicative, and confirm anything you
      intend to rely on against the Land Department directly. We do not warrant
      that any figure is current.
    </p>
    <p>
      Where the underlying record is thin we do not publish a median at all
      rather than publish an unreliable one, which is why parts of the map carry
      no figure. An absent number is a deliberate answer, not a gap.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin-top: var(--space-l);">Third-party names</h2>
    <p style="margin-top: var(--space-s);">
      Authorities, banks and developers are referred to descriptively, to explain
      how a transaction works. Those names belong to their owners, and reference
      does not imply affiliation or endorsement in either direction.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin-top: var(--space-l);">Liability</h2>
    <p style="margin-top: var(--space-s);">
      This site is provided as it is. To the extent the law allows, we are not
      liable for loss arising from decisions taken on the basis of it. That is
      not an attempt to disclaim carelessness on our part: it is an
      acknowledgement that a published median cannot know the property in front
      of you, and that the person who can is the one you should be paying.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
